      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T07:58:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s generally confusing to have equals and hashCode ignore fields that are part of the object\u0027s semantics. I\u0027ve really only seen this done for fields that are transient and non-meaninfgul (e.g., caches, temoprary calculated values, and the like).\n\nIf you want to only compare some of the fields, would suggest not storing the duration in the object at all. Or, if there are some cases where the duration doesn\u0027t matter, you could add another method such as \"boolean hasSameVirtualInterfacesAs(MfcValue other)\".",
